  {
    "id": "0625a4ac-475e-508a-9a32-f2bc4ce01ffd",
    "pack": "advanced-players-guide",
    "kind": "equipment",
    "slug": "equipment:pilgrims-token",
    "name": "Pilgrim's Token",
    "level": 0,
    "rarity": "common",
    "traits": [],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "advanced-players-guide",
        "aon": "https://2e.aonprd.com/Feats.aspx?ID=2141"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A small token of protection from a site holy to your faith, or you touched your religious symbol to a relic or altar at such a site. So long as this token is in your possession, when you tie an adversary's initiative roll, you go first."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Special",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " If you select the "
          },
          {
            "type": "ref",
            "id": "7049e802-66ba-5a75-8c0a-b4abd2412b65"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " feat at 1st level, you receive your pilgrim's token for free. Alternately, if you have a religious symbol, it is already attuned, as described above."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "If you select this feat at a later level, or if you lose your pilgrim's token, you must purchase or Craft a replacement and attune it at a holy site. Such a token usually costs at least 2 sp, and the attunement takes 10 minutes of prayer and requires a successful "
          },
          {
            "type": "check",
            "statistic": "skill:religion",
            "dc": 20
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " check. Your GM might adjust the price and DC depending on the token's material and quality and the religious significance of the site; the more significant the location, the easier the attunement."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "externalIds": {
      "foundry": "Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.gwP3Uums2ApH6o9K"
    },
    "data": {
      "price": {
        "coins": {
          "sp": 2
        }
      },
      "bulk": "negligible",
      "usage": {
        "type": "worn"
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "21dd4af9-95cf-5f79-b481-964affd15e0c",
    "pack": "advanced-players-guide",
    "kind": "equipment",
    "slug": "equipment:predictable-silver-piece",
    "name": "Predictable Silver Piece",
    "level": 1,
    "rarity": "common",
    "traits": ["magical"],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "advanced-players-guide",
        "aon": "https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=740"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This seemingly unremarkable, weathered silver coin bears the bust of an unnamed monarch on the face and a majestic bird on the tail. You can toss the coin without activating it, in which case it follows the normal laws of probability."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Activate",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " "
          },
          {
            "type": "action-cost",
            "cost": "one"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " Interact"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Effect",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " You rub your thumb on one side of the coin with the intent of slightly tweaking the strands of fate, then flip the coin into the air in a coin toss. No matter how the toss is resolved- letting the coin fall to the ground, slapping it down on the back of your hand, or catching it on your open palm-it always lands with the side you rubbed face up."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "externalIds": {
      "foundry": "Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.ZIQAzOavTXJCcCMD"
    },
    "data": {
      "price": {
        "coins": {
          "gp": 3
        }
      },
      "bulk": "negligible",
      "usage": {
        "type": "held",
        "hands": "one"
      }
    }
  },
  {
